  \item A doubly linked unsorted list.
  \item A singly linked sorted list.
  \item A doubly linked sorted list.
\end{itemize}

\textit{Solution:} Two different issues must be considered in evaluating these implementations: singly vs. doubly linked lists and sorted vs. unsorted order. Operations with subtle implementations are denoted with an asterisk:

\begin{table}[ht]
