\subsection{SSL Protocol Architecture}
SSL adds an extra layer between the Transport and Application layers, and some special application protocols in the Application layer, as shown in Fig. 8.14. The extra layer implements SSL's \textit{Record protocol}, which provides basic encryption and integrity services for applications. The new application protocols control the operation of the record protocol:

